{
  "title": "Grokked Transformers are Implicit Reasoners",
  "authors": [
    "Boshi Wang",
    "Xiang Yue",
    "Yu Su",
    "Huan Sun"
  ],
  "year": 2024,
  "arxivId": "2405.15071",
  "abstract": "This paper explores whether transformers can learn to reason implicitly over parametric knowledge. The authors find that transformers can learn implicit reasoning through extended training, known as grokking, but the level of generalization varies across different reasoning types. The study reveals the mechanism behind grokking and suggests potential improvements to the transformer architecture.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "Transformers can learn to reason implicitly, but this skill is only acquired through <strong>grokking</strong>, a phenomenon where the model is trained far beyond overfitting. The level of generalization also varies across different reasoning types, such as composition and comparison.",
