    {
      "title": "The Results",
      "content": "The authors find that the transformer can learn to reason implicitly, but the level of generalization varies across different reasoning types. For composition, the model fails to generalize to out-of-distribution examples, while for comparison, the model achieves systematic generalization. The results also show that the speed of improvement in generalization correlates with the ratio between inferred and atomic facts in training.",
